-- emit: whole-program specialisation's definite initialisation
-- (`backend.md` §9, *Slice 4*, amended 2026-10-03), in a platform module
-- (`platform/Inst.beni`) written as the browser runtime writes `unit` and
-- `patch`:
--
--   * a kind's `m` returns an instance as an object literal with no `b`,
--     and the one call of `m` — `unit`'s — writes `t` and then `b` in the
--     statements right after it, before anything can read them: `b` exists
--     from the moment the instance does, so `patch`'s read of it is the one
--     module-level block `unit` was shown, never `undefined`, and `patch`
--     says "same" with no test (and, nothing else reading them, `unit`'s
--     two writes go);
--   * `bare`'s literal is returned by a function also called where nothing
--     writes `b` after the call: `shows` keeps its comparison.
import Inst
import Node


main : Node.Program
main = Node.printLines (Inst.demo ())
